  "tier": "sol",
  "complexity": 5,
  "title": "T1: spawn.render validates placeholders against the template with single-pass substitution; dispatch, fresh-fix dispatch and run_worker hold on render errors with hold_reason render_error",
  "spec": "What: make prompt rendering robust to values that quote the double-brace placeholder syntax, and make every render failure a visible hold instead of a silent death.\nWhy: spawn.render (orchestrator/spawn.py:101-113) substitutes each keyword sequentially with str.replace and then raises ValueError unfilled_placeholder for ANY double-brace token left in the rendered text. A spec, acceptance line or diff that merely quotes a placeholder therefore raises; and a value that contains another key's token is substituted twice. The exception escapes daemon.dispatch in the tick thread (orchestrator/daemon.py:852-856, render runs before spawn_async and before complete(dispatched_at)) so the task is re-stamped every lease with no event; in daemon._dispatch_fresh_fix (daemon.py:554-563) and spawn.run_worker (spawn.py:757-779, render happens after pool.pick but before bus.claim) the worker thread dies silently and the task stays queued.\n1. spawn.render: collect the set of placeholder names in the RAW template (same regex as today, before any substitution). missing = template tokens not in kw -> raise ValueError with the same message form unfilled_placeholder: <name> (first missing name). Then substitute in ONE pass with re.sub and a callback that looks each token up in kw (str values verbatim, other values json.dumps indent=0 as today). Tokens inside substituted values are never touched. Keep the existing packet-required check and scout defaults unchanged. Extra keyword arguments not present in the template stay silently ignored (today's behaviour).\n2. daemon.dispatch execute path (daemon.py:852-856): wrap spawn.packet + spawn.render in try/except Exception; on error call a new helper daemon.hold_render_error(task_id, exc) and continue with the next candidate (never let the tick raise). The helper: under bus.locked(), set status held, hold_reason \"render_error: \" + str(exc)[:200], pipeline.render_error = str(exc)[:300], pop pipeline.dispatched_at; then notify.notify(f\"{task_id}: render_error: {exc}\"). Same wrapping in _dispatch_fresh_fix (daemon.py:554-563). Existing hold_failed stays as is.\n3. spawn.run_worker (spawn.py:757-779): wrap the role render branch in try/except Exception -> same hold (status held, hold_reason \"render_error: ...\", pipeline.render_error, notify) via a small local helper in spawn.py (spawn must not import daemon), return {\"status\": \"held\", \"reason\": \"render_error\"} before pool.reserve/bus.claim.\n4. daemon.auto_fix_round (daemon.py:141-): skip any held task whose hold_reason starts with \"render_error\" (a spec defect the Planner repairs; never a fix round).\nKeep tests/test_spawn.py::test_render_flags_unfilled_placeholder (missing packet still raises \"unfilled_placeholder: packet\") and tests/test_daemon.py::test_dispatch_prompt_contains_packet_not_placeholder green. Do not write any literal double-brace token into task specs or titles in tests; build such strings in test code. No new dependencies.",
  "inputs": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_spawn.py::test_render_validates_against_template_not_output \u2014 render('execute', packet='p', spec=<a string that quotes the acceptance placeholder in double braces>, acceptance=['a'], scope=['x.py']) succeeds and the output contains that quoted token verbatim exactly once; render('execute', spec='s', acceptance=['a'], scope=['x.py']) still raises ValueError matching 'unfilled_placeholder: packet'",
    "tests/test_spawn.py::test_render_single_pass_never_resubstitutes \u2014 with spec set to a string containing the scope placeholder token and scope=['z.py'], the rendered text contains the literal spec token and the substituted scope exactly where the template places them, and json.dumps of scope appears exactly once",
    "tests/test_daemon.py::test_dispatch_holds_execute_task_on_render_error \u2014 a queued execute task with spawn.render patched to raise ValueError('unfilled_placeholder: spec') ends status held, hold_reason startswith 'render_error: unfilled_placeholder', pipeline.render_error set, no pipeline.dispatched_at, one notify line containing the task id, and daemon.dispatch(pool) returns without raising while a second normal queued execute task in the same tick is still dispatched",
    "tests/test_daemon.py::test_fresh_fix_dispatch_holds_on_render_error \u2014 daemon._dispatch_fresh_fix(task_id, 'compat_changed:x') with spawn.render raising leaves the task held with hold_reason startswith 'render_error' and does not call _dispatch_worker",
    "tests/test_spawn.py::test_run_worker_holds_on_render_error \u2014 spawn.run_worker for a queued review task whose render raises returns {'status': 'held', ...}, the task is held with hold_reason startswith 'render_error', assigned_to is None (never claimed) and notify was called",
    "tests/test_daemon.py::test_auto_fix_round_skips_render_error_hold \u2014 a held execute task with hold_reason 'render_error: unfilled_placeholder: spec' gets no fix-round child after daemon.auto_fix_round(pool)"
  ],
